    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0177" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg177"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Lyons to Mr. Seward</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">British
                            Legation</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                                C.</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-10-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 11, 1861</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to you a copy
                    of a memorial addressed to Earl Russell, her Majesty’s principal secretary of
                    state for foreign affairs, by Mr. William Gray, owner of the British ship
                    “Perthshire,” which appears to have been interfered with by United States
                    ships-of-war. I am directed by Lord Russell to ask the government of the United
                    States for an explanation.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, sir, your most obedient, humble
                    servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. H. Seward</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d106-a1.xml" xpointer="d106-a1"/>
            </div>
